#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 840.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186163010} :activity/id #uuid "4a097ed8-748d-54f4-a06d-fefa2b69e0d1" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049206 :topic/id #uuid "e354e91d-75ea-5244-818d-ff4a2cb8189e" :topic/math-academy-id 3050} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186163010 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186163294 :tutorial/content "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two random variables with covariance $\\textrm{Cov}[X, Y]$ and standard deviations $\\textrm {SD}[X]$ and $\\textrm {SD}[Y].$ \n\nThe **correlation coefficient of $X$ and $Y,$** also known as the **Pearson correlation coefficient**, is denoted $\\rho$ (the Greek letter \"rho\") and is defined as\n\n$$\n\\rho = \\dfrac{\\textrm{Cov}[X, Y] }{\\textrm {SD}[X]\\cdot \\textrm {SD}[Y]}.\n$$\n\nNote the following:\n\n- The correlation coefficient satisfies\n\n$$\n-1\\leq \\rho \\leq 1.\n$$\n\n- If $X$ and $Y$ are independent random variables, then \n\n$$\n\\rho = 0.\n$$\n\nThe reverse implication does not always hold. In other words, $\\rho=0$ does *not* imply that $X$ and $Y$ are independent.\n\n- Unlike the covariance, $\\rho$ is a *dimensionless* quantity. This means we'll get the same answer regardless of the units used to measure $X$ and $Y.$\n\n- Also unlike the covariance, $\\rho$ tells the strength of the correlation between $X$ and $Y.$ We typically have the following rule of thumb:\n\n- If $|\\rho| \\gt 0.7,$ the correlation is **strong,** and the data generated by our two random variables closely follow a straight line. \n\n![](images/3f/3fd8b4e85bd76bbf78fdb2b135c49b3fd5e37fd9651dcae29d945d75aa45b905.png)\n\n- If $0.3\\leq |\\rho| \\leq 0.7,$ the correlation is **weak.** The data generated by our random variables follow a straight line, but many are far from the line.\n\n![](images/c1/c132ec90770bb84ad6c7dcc4b24773a923139c616f523ba0a23c1506c40c508c.png)\n\n- If $|\\rho| \\lt 0.3,$ then the correlation is **negligible.** No (linear) correlation exists between the data points generated by the random variables.\n\n![](images/9a/9afa80bfadc40b8b832b17dcea10d66d5a08955909d5bea66c7c010558b5ea19.png)\n\nLet's get some practice computing the correlation coefficient." :tutorial/id #uuid "96cc345f-656a-5faf-a2cf-47946504320d" :tutorial/math-academy-id 5638 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "5afd6705-a870-5fc5-8b7c-544c322a2815" :step/math-academy-id 34624 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186163121}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186163121 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162140 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161706 :question/id #uuid "284f65cd-1288-56ed-80b7-f611b1464835" :question/math-academy-id "e-10372"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b371f15-7541-5cd9-ac1c-e53fd3b8fc18" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048424} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050351}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162440} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162441} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186546966} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186546969} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186546972} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186547017}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Correlation Coefficient Given Variances and Covariance"} :step/id #uuid "f053d13a-ebb8-5437-aa41-81a2459e4c6d" :step/math-academy-id 39086 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186163122}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186163122 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162141 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161707 :question/id #uuid "d132664b-222c-5dd5-a52b-2471d10fcb25" :question/math-academy-id "e-10373"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c5fab7dc-3857-5840-a349-6d90e5f6e280" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162442} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162446} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416506} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186547020} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186547024}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Correlation Coefficient of Two Discrete Random Variables"} :step/id #uuid "ba6783eb-c401-5b3d-aa3b-85965b1f3255" :step/math-academy-id 39089 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186163123}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186163123 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162142 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161708 :question/id #uuid "6562853a-696d-5cb5-a79d-76ff1a084d90" :question/math-academy-id "e-10384"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "51a3f265-d2dd-5e62-931e-4bf6d7597ea4" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162443} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162447} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186546977} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186546989} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186547013} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186547028} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186547063}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Correlation Coefficient of Two Continuous Random Variables"} :step/id #uuid "083a778d-72e3-562d-b4fc-a52938de9b8b" :step/math-academy-id 39123}] :activity/title "The Correlation Coefficient for Two Random Variables" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186162188}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046660} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416508} :activity/id #uuid "73500361-3c8f-52ce-8bc5-0eba17f74db0" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049206 :topic/id #uuid "e354e91d-75ea-5244-818d-ff4a2cb8189e" :topic/math-academy-id 3050} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416507 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416506 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0876eb83-57bd-5e84-8477-dc5d60ce323d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416488} {:answer/id #uuid "54445a12-3783-54c9-a829-54a3a211f3e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-0.53" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416489} {:answer/id #uuid "59e0c0fc-3c74-57a4-869c-4fa2f31bf145" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-0.21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416490} {:answer/id #uuid "90d7f216-f436-5ba1-90e3-d380e7bb6856" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-0.02" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416497} {:answer/id #uuid "c5c6d741-b8ea-5c6d-a797-e6668be9d1b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416500}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416497} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3019da1-a157-5528-94a6-85caf91d61fd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416503}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "71621138-ed93-53b4-9ace-266f4a0d5dab" :question/math-academy-id "q-148377" :question/problem "| $f(x,y)$ | $Y=-4$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.16$ | $0.17$ | $0.19$ | $0.52$ |\n| $X=10$ | $0.15$ | $0.17$ | $0.16$ | $0.48$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.31$ | $0.34$ | $0.35$ | $1$ |\n\nThe joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is shown above. Given that \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=4.8,\\,\\text{E}[Y]=-0.54,\\,\\text{SD}[X]≈4.9960,\\,\\text{SD}[Y]≈2.4634,\n$$\n\n \nfind the correlation coefficient of $X$ and $Y.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the correlation coefficient of random variables $X$ and $Y$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\rho =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]$ is the covariance, and\n\n- $\\text{SD}[X]$ and $\\text{SD}[Y]$ are the standard deviations of $X$ and $Y.$\n\nFirst, by applying the rule of the lazy statistician, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[XY] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}{\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{Y}}xy\\,f(x,y) \\\\  & =0\\cdot (-4)\\cdot 0.16+0\\cdot 0\\cdot 0.17+0\\cdot 2\\cdot 0.19 \\\\  & +10\\cdot (-4)\\cdot 0.15+10\\cdot 0\\cdot 0.17+10\\cdot 2\\cdot 0.16 \\\\  & =-2.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the covariance and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =-2.8-(4.8)(-0.54) \\\\  & =-0.208.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correlation coefficient is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\rho  & =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]} \\\\  & ≈\\frac{-0.208}{4.9960\\cdot 2.4634} \\\\  & ≈-0.02,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places."} :step/id #uuid "64154ed0-ecd2-5a93-a53c-c88a0fff494a"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416508 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162442 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6835da4f-0783-54f5-9112-499b793c7b69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-0.32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416492} {:answer/id #uuid "7d3b6071-447a-5e5b-955a-60e039ddb364" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-0.23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416494} {:answer/id #uuid "84a27511-2f73-51ad-9efc-512adfb8573b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.38" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416496} {:answer/id #uuid "f032cbc3-7ec5-5ffd-9b44-86c708965b4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.61" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416501} {:answer/id #uuid "f2544fdb-11f6-5f6b-b648-844f55f4831f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-0.16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416502}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416494} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd07d7b1-6cdf-5103-98fc-8aa75014e305" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416505}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "86b78d29-f123-58f2-82ad-24e8b4486f2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-146471" :question/problem "| $f(x,y)$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.4$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.3$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.6$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.4$ | $0.2$ | $0.4$ | $1$ |\n\nThe joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is shown above. Given that \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=0.6,\\,\\text{E}[Y]=1,\\,\\text{SD}[X]≈0.4899,\\,\\text{SD}[Y]≈0.8944,\n$$\n\n \nfind the correlation coefficient of $X$ and $Y.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Recall that the correlation coefficient of random variables $X$ and $Y$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\rho =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]$ is the covariance, and\n\n- $\\text{SD}[X]$ and $\\text{SD}[Y]$ are the standard deviations of $X$ and $Y.$\n\nFirst, by applying the rule of the lazy statistician, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[XY] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}{\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{Y}}xy\\,f(x,y) \\\\  & =0\\cdot 0\\cdot 0.1+0\\cdot 1\\cdot 0.1+0\\cdot 2\\cdot 0.2 \\\\  & +1\\cdot 0\\cdot 0.3+1\\cdot 1\\cdot 0.1+1\\cdot 2\\cdot 0.2 \\\\  & =0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the covariance and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =0.5-(0.6)(1) \\\\  & =-0.1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correlation coefficient is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\rho  & =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]} \\\\  & ≈\\frac{-0.1}{0.4899\\cdot 0.8944} \\\\  & ≈0.23,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places."} :step/id #uuid "a8c3d0f3-7ae4-57cd-aeb8-05d8cdcf0700" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416509}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416509 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162446 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "671ca342-974b-595d-90ce-f2d135a933c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416491} {:answer/id #uuid "76b4ff69-0d3b-5cf8-8bc0-c37eb66140b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416493} {:answer/id #uuid "8305d7f0-359a-5672-84b3-d2451cec6023" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-0.60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416495} {:answer/id #uuid "92d2fd3c-8d02-57f3-80c7-ad19c8e18d56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-0.36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416498} {:answer/id #uuid "990379fa-9ca9-5e21-9b76-b06e960628cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-0.22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416499}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416498} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7baad12-38b1-5f0c-9519-c9cab1926772" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416504}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "972ce393-9eba-55fd-8649-cb51968b297d" :question/math-academy-id "q-148368" :question/problem "| $f(x,y)$ | $Y=-1$ | $Y=1$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.2$ | $0.5$ | $0.7$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.3$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.4$ | $0.6$ | $1$ |\n\nThe joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is shown above. Given that \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=0.3\\,\\text{E}[Y]=0.2,\\,\\text{SD}[X]≈0.4583,\\,\\text{SD}[Y]≈0.9798,\n$$\n\n \nfind the correlation coefficient of $X$ and $Y.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Recall that the correlation coefficient of random variables $X$ and $Y$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\rho =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]$ is the covariance, and\n\n- $\\text{SD}[X]$ and $\\text{SD}[Y]$ are the standard deviations of $X$ and $Y.$\n\nFirst, by applying the rule of the lazy statistician, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[XY] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}{\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{Y}}xy\\,f(x,y) \\\\  & =0\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 0.2+0\\cdot 1\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & +1\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 0.2+1\\cdot 1\\cdot 0.1 \\\\  & =-0.1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the covariance and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =-0.1-(0.3)(0.2) \\\\  & =-0.16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correlation coefficient is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\rho  & =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]} \\\\  & ≈\\frac{-0.16}{0.4583\\cdot 0.9798} \\\\  & ≈-0.36,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places."} :step/id #uuid "c917e351-229c-5962-9db6-66543286f0e6" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416507}}] :activity/title "The Correlation Coefficient for Two Random Variables" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416487}]}
